WEBVTT

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.363
A donor cannot afford this month's gift.

00:00:03.363 --> 00:00:08.123
Pledge Line completes eligible hardship relief after the donor approves the exact request.

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:15.715
The sponsor's twenty-five dollar capture completes first.

00:00:15.715 --> 00:00:19.047
Then the donor's twenty-five dollar charge is refunded.

00:00:19.047 --> 00:00:21.129
Their monthly gift remains active.

00:00:21.129 --> 00:00:22.379
Fees still apply.

00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:29.446
The same nonprofit needs one hundred shirts under eight hundred dollars.

00:00:29.446 --> 00:00:30.713
Anthropic proposes counteroffers.

00:00:30.713 --> 00:00:31.557
Jev reviews.

00:00:31.557 --> 00:00:34.936
Code checks the complete allocation and its limits.

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:41.805
The buyer approves an exact six hundred seventy-six dollar, twenty-five cent plan.

00:00:41.805 --> 00:00:47.226
Two PayPal sandbox captures complete, with one create and capture attempt per supplier.

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:51.298
The app restarts between supplier payments.

00:00:51.298 --> 00:00:54.213
The original browser recovers the partial order.

00:00:54.213 --> 00:00:58.377
The signed donor receipt remains verifiable after restart and redeployment.

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:04.397
These are recorded sandbox outcomes, not live payments.

00:01:04.397 --> 00:01:07.993
Suppliers are controlled lab processes, without independent fulfillment.

00:01:07.993 --> 00:01:12.489
Explore the receipts and exact financial evidence in Pledge Line.
